n   Reduction percentage = P = (R / O) * 100\n\n2. Given values:\n   O = 120\n   N = 96\n\n3. Calculate the reduction amount:\n   R = O - N\n   R = 120 - 96\n   R = 24\n\n4. Calculate the reduction percentage:\n   P = (R / O) * 100\n   P = (24 / 120) * 100\n   P = 0.2 * 100\n   P = 20%\n\nTherefore, the reduction percent is 20%.\n\nThe answer is C."], "Programming ExpertsDGv": ["```python\n\ndef reduction_percent():\n    original_value = 120\n    new_value = 96\n    reduction_amount = original_value - new_value\n    reduction_percent = (reduction_amount / original_value) * 100\n    return reduction_percent\n\nanswer = reduction_percent()\n\nprint(answer)\n\n```\nthe answer is 20.0"], "InspectorfuGw": ["To solve this problem, I will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the reduction amount:\n   Reduction amount = Original amount - New amount\n   Reduction amount = 120 - 96\n   Reduction amount = 24\n\n2. Calculate the reduction percent:\n   Reduction percent = (Reduction amount / Original amount) * 100\n   Reduction percent = (24 / 120) * 100\n   Reduction percent = 0.2 * 100\n   Reduction percent = 20%\n\nThe reduction percent is 20%. \n\nThe answer is C."], "Math SolverSn9k": ["To find the reduction percent, I'll follow these steps:\n\nStep 1: Calculate the reduction amount\nReduction amount = Original amount - New amount\n= 120 - 96\n= 24\n\nStep 2: Calculate the reduction percent\nReduction percent = (Reduction amount / Original amount) \u00d7 100\n= (24 / 120) \u00d7 100\n= 20%\n\nTherefore, the reduction percent is 20%."]}], "Response": ["C"], "Attempt answer": "C", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 28, "Total executed": 43, "Accuracy": 0.6511627906976745}
